ges and a private, residents-only portal to ensure security and ease of access.\\\\n\\\\n**A. Public Pages (Accessible to all visitors)**\\\\n\\\\n*   **/home**: Welcome message, excerpts of latest announcements, and a prominent login button.\\\\n*   **/about**: Information on the HOA, the community, and current board members.\\\\n*   **/documents**: Access to non-sensitive, public-facing documents (e.g., Bylaws, Covenants).\\\\n*   **/contact**: Contact form for general inquiries and management company details.\\\\n\\\\n**B. Resident Portal (Requires login)**\\\\n\\\\n*   **/portal/dashboard**: The landing page after login, showing a full feed of announcements and an event calendar.\\\\n*   **/portal/documents**: A secure repository for sensitive documents, categorized for clarity (e.g., Meeting Minutes, Financials).\\\\n*   **/portal/directory**: An opt-in resident directory to respect privacy.\\\\n*   **/portal/profile**: Allows residents to view and update their contact information.\\\\n\\\\n**C. Admin Functions (Accessible only to Admin-level users)**\\\\n\\\\n*   **User Management**: Add, edit, or deactivate resident accounts.\\\\n*   **Content Management**: Create/edit announcements, upload/manage documents, and manage calendar events.\\\\n\\\\n### **2. Key User Flows**\\\\n\\\\n**A. Flow: Resident Views a Protected Document**\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Navigate & Login:** The resident visits the homepage, clicks \\\\\\\"Login,\\\\\\\" and enters their credentials.\\\\n2.  **Authentication:** Upon successful login, the system directs them to the Resident Portal Dashboard.\\\\n3.  **Access Documents:** The resident clicks the \\\\\\\"Secure Documents\\\\\\\" link in the portal navigation.\\\\n4.  **Select Document:** The resident browses the categories and clicks on the desired file.\\\\n5.  **View:** The system presents the document for viewing or download.\\\\n\\\\n**B. Flow: Administrator Posts a New Update**\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Navigate & Login:** The administrator logs in